# Optional: `k dev` needs no .env. Without DATABASE_URL it uses a SQLite file
# at .k/huddle.db (git-ignored), created and migrated at startup. Copy this to
# .env (git-ignored) only to use another database. `.env` is read only in
# development; production reads the real process environment, and `k test`
# reads neither. Format: docs/design/25-config-and-secrets.md. `dist/app
# config` lists every variable a build reads, the channels' limits included.

# Another SQLite file:
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:.k/other.db

# Push notifications (docs/design/50-push.md): the app's own VAPID key, from
# `k keys new p256-ecdsa` (the private JWK it prints). Without it the rooms'
# "Notify me" switch isn't shown.
# K_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY={"kty":"EC","crv":"P-256",...}
# K_PUSH_CONTACT=mailto:you@example.com
